DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aammddppmm driver provides support for the AMD-756/766/768/8111 Power Man‐
     agement controller.

     The RNG function of the AMD-768/8111 Power Management controller is sup‐
     ported.  Data generated by the RNG get fed into the pool of the random(4)
     device.

     The SMBus host interface of the AMD-756/766/768/8111 Power Management
     controller and NVIDIA nForce 1 chipset are also supported.  The SMBus
     host interface can be used with the iic(4) framework.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     iic(4), intro(4), pci(4), random(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aammddppmm device driver appeared in OpenBSD 3.2.  SMBus host interface
     support was added in OpenBSD 3.9.

